{"type":"step-attempt","step":"code-review","sessionId":"e39cd91f-a90f-423b-89a4-76db98ef6a33","outcome":{"verdict":"needs-fix","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/optional-github-integration/review-feedback-002.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"findings":[{"severity":"high","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/cli/bootstrap.ts","title":"bootstrap re-derives github.enabled from current config instead of job state (D1 / TC-011 violation)","rationale":"bootstrap() calls resolveGitHubIntegrationConfig(config) which reads the current project config. If the config was changed from github.enabled:false to true after a job was started, the resume path would resolve a GitHub token and inject it into git transport via createTransportAuth, violating TC-030 (zero token resolutions) and TC-031 (no extraheader injection) for that disabled job. D1 requires resume/reopen/attach/archive to use the stored job state's githubIntegration.enabled, not the current config.","line":43,"remediation":{"invariant":"resume / reopen / attach / archive must derive githubEnabled from getGitHubIntegration(state).enabled (job state), not from resolveGitHubIntegrationConfig(config) (current config).","sites":[{"file":"src/cli/bootstrap.ts","line":43},{"file":"src/cli/resume.ts","line":63}],"approach":"In resume.ts, call getGitHubIntegration(state).enabled to get the job's contract value and pass it as an optional override to bootstrap(). bootstrap() should accept a githubEnabledOverride parameter; when provided, use it instead of re-reading from config. This makes the job state authoritative per D1 without breaking the run (new-job) path that reads from config."}},{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/core/command/runner.ts","title":"Completion output for GitHub-disabled jobs omits final revision OID and attestation path (TC-051 unimplemented; JSON contract missing D7 additive fields)","rationale":"TC-051 (must) requires the human-readable completion output to show 'feature branch / 最終 revision / 証跡パスが表示せ'. The current handleResult only logs the branch name; it does not display the final commit OID (state.synthesizedCommits.at(-1)) or the attestation file path. Additionally, design D7 prescribes adding branch/revision/githubIntegration as additive fields to RunResultContract for machine consumers, but those fields are absent from the interface and buildRunResult implementation. No test covers the branch-published result path in run-result.test.ts.","line":469,"remediation":{"invariant":"For GitHub-disabled awaiting-archive jobs, handleResult must display the final commit OID and attestation path; buildRunResult must include branch/revision/githubIntegration additive fields in the JSON contract.","sites":[{"file":"src/core/command/runner.ts","line":469},{"file":"src/core/command/run-result.ts","line":16}],"approach":"In handleResult, after 'Branch published: ...', add logInfo for the final OID from state.synthesizedCommits?.at(-1) (skip when null) and the attestation path when the file exists. In RunResultContract, add optional branch?: string, revision?: string, githubIntegration?: { enabled: boolean } fields. In buildRunResult, populate these from state.branch, state.synthesizedCommits?.at(-1), and state.githubIntegration when result === 'branch-published'. Add unit tests for the branch-published case in run-result.test.ts."}},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/config/github-integration.ts","title":"Redundant null check in traceGitHubIntegration","rationale":"The outer if condition already checks projectLocalRaw !== null (line 48), then the inner typeof check includes another projectLocalRaw !== null (line 50) that is dead code. Minor readability issue; no correctness impact.","line":50,"remediation":{"invariant":"Each variable should be null-checked at most once within the same conditional scope.","sites":[{"file":"src/config/github-integration.ts","line":50}],"approach":"Remove the redundant projectLocalRaw !== null check on the inner line (line 50). The outer guard on line 48 is sufficient."}}],"evidence":{"checked":47,"skipped":3,"unverified":2},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"tests/unit/state/github-integration.test.ts","title":"TC-011 unit test verifies the accessor but not the resume CLI integration path","rationale":"The test correctly verifies that getGitHubIntegration reads from the state field. It does not exercise the resume.ts → bootstrap.ts path where the config re-read happens. Fixing F-1 should be accompanied by an integration test that simulates a config change between start and resume.","line":81}]},"followUpAttempts":1,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":1}},"startedAt":"2026-09-06T14:29:37.637Z","endedAt":"2026-09-06T14:37:08.030Z","commitOid":"8df2b9a2276e1746bddebecb2af2d7664f70847d"}
